--- frontend/src/renderer/hooks/useConversation.ts:2227 ---
👮 **Wachiman** · 🟡⚡ **Consider · perf: The old-daemon fallback is not remembered per host, unlike the PR description (confidence medium)**

The PR body says that on `ROUTE_NOT_FOUND` "the app then falls back to the full list and remembers that host", and lists a test for "the old-daemon fallback that's remembered per host". `fetchWorkspaceFilePaths` keeps no state: every call first requests `/workspace/paths` and, on a 404, issues `/workspace/files` as well. For a remote host on an older daemon, `useWorkspaceFilePaths` refetches every 30 s (line 2251) and also on each workspace file-change invalidation, so each refresh pays an extra failed request on top of the slow full-list read this PR is trying to avoid. The new test (`useConversation.file-paths.test.ts:49`) only checks that the fallback result is correct, not that it is remembered. Either cache the unsupported host (for example a `Set` keyed by `hostId`, cleared on reconnect) or correct the description.

<!-- wachi:finding -->
--- frontend/src/renderer/routes/_shell.projects.$projectId_.sessions.$sessionId.tsx:24 ---
👮 **Wachiman** · 🟠🐛 **Fix · bug: Loader prefetch also runs on hover preload, contrary to the PR description (confidence medium)**

The PR body says the conversation read starts in the loader "on navigation (not on hover preload)". The loader ignores TanStack's `preload` flag, and the router sets `defaultPreload: "intent"` (`frontend/src/renderer/router.tsx:21`), so the loader runs when a sidebar row is hovered and `prefetchChat` fires `prefetchInfiniteQuery` for every hovered chat. Those requests compete for the same 6 per-host connections this PR is trying to free, and users sweeping the mouse down the sidebar start one conversation read per row. Take `preload` from the loader args and skip `prefetchChat` when it is true, or change the description if hover prefetch is intended.

